==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|eo}} {{term|habere|habēre|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|habeo|habeō|have, hold, possess|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{eo-verb|hav}}

# to [[have]]
#: Mi '''havas''' elektran torĉon, sed mi ne '''havas''' bateriojn.
#: I have a flashlight, but I don't have batteries.

====Derived terms====

* [[bonhava]]: [[well-to-do]], [[affluent]]
* [[bonhavo]]:  [[affluence]]
* [[enhaveco]]: [[capacity]]
* [[enhavi]]: to [[contain]], to [[comprise]], to [[include]]
* [[enhavo]]: [[contents]], [[table of contents]]
* [[hava]]:  [[comfortable]] (not needy); [[well off]]
* [[havigi]]: to [[supply]], to [[provide]]
* [[havo]], [[havaĵo]]:  [[possession]]
* [[malhava]], [[senhava]]:  to be [[destitute]], to be [[penniless]]
* [[malhavi]], [[senhavi]]: to [[lack]]
* [[senhavigi]]:  to [[deprive]]

